From 75a18764d0758ee2a6b8336d0b59898538dc9daf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: curnane-lab <curnane-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:55:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(gdn): recover startup capability probe, records dump
 hook, phase ledger

- assert_recover_capability(): before any graph capture, run a fixed
  on-device case (permuted + request-shared record rows) and check the
  effective records cells against an fp64 CPU reference (key bit-exact,
  dc/alpha within the frozen tolerances), untouched-row sentinels, and
  bitwise out/state parity with the stock entry.  Any mismatch raises and
  refuses startup: with the wheel OPP ahead of the R1 OPP the recover entry
  launches but writes wrong records (N10), so symbol resolution alone is not
  sufficient.  recover_available() now runs the probe.
- VLLM_ASCEND_GDN_RECOVER_DUMP=<dir>: dump every verify call's inputs,
  pre-call read-row states and the records snapshot for offline oracle
  checks (eager mode only; under graph capture the python call site runs
  once, at capture time).
- Bucket the private-runtime launch counters by phase (pre_capture /
  capture / post_capture_eager) and expose them in workspace_report().

Signed-off-by: curnane-lab <curnane-lab@users.noreply.github.com>
